---
description: Repository, branch, database, and deployment constraints for the FAW migration
alwaysApply: true
---

- Work only in the Azure DevOps repository `WebFaw-Flutterflow`.
- Keep the migration work on branch `faw-react`; do not switch to or push migration commits to `master` or `master.deploy`.
- The only application database is PostgreSQL through `@payloadcms/db-postgres`.
- Production deploys run through `azure-pipelines.yml` and target Railway project `faw-trucks`, environment `production`, service `faw-web`.
- Preserve concurrent user and agent changes. Inspect the working tree before editing, and do not reset, clean, force-push, or overwrite unrelated work.
